  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "I found two settled card payments to TechMart Online for EUR 240.00 each:\n\n- **TX-0402**, 14 July 2026\n- **TX-0401**, 20 July 2026\n\nI can't see the merchant's side, so I can't tell from the account alone whether the second payment is a duplicate or a separate purchase. The right dispute reason depends on what happened:\n\n1. **Duplicate charge:** you were charged twice for the same purchase. This would apply if the two payments were for one order.\n2. **Service or goods not received:** you paid for something you didn't receive or that wasn't delivered. This would apply if the payment(s) were for something that never arrived.\n3. **Unauthorized debit or card-not-present fraud:** you didn't make one of these payments. Tell me if this applies.\n\nWhich of these matches your situation? Once you tell me, I'll check whether the transaction is eligible for a dispute. I won't open anything until you confirm.",
